urefooted",r=3,max=3},{tree="SV",name=S[590],r=5,max=5},{tree="SV",name=S[591],r=2,max=2},{tree="SV",name="Expose Prey",r=2,max=2},{tree="SV",name=S[410],r=2,max=2},{tree="SV",name=S[411],r=1,max=1},{tree="SV",name=S[534],r=5,max=5},{tree="SV",name=S[535],r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=14,tree="SV",name=S[298],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=15,l2=19,tree="SV",name="Survivalist",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=20,l2=22,tree="SV",name="Surefooted",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=23,l2=24,tree="SV",name=S[615],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=25,l2=29,tree="SV",name=S[590],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=30,l2=30,tree="SV",name=S[411],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=31,l2=32,tree="SV",name="Expose Prey",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=34,tree="SV",name=S[591],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=35,l2=39,tree="SV",name=S[534],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="SV",name=S[535],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=42,tree="SV",name=S[668],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=43,l2=44,tree="SV",name=S[410],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=45,l2=49,tree="MM",name=S[210],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=50,l2=54,tree="MM",name="Careful Aim",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=55,l2=55,tree="MM",name="Lone Wolf",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=56,l2=60,tree="BM",name=S[339],r1=1,r2=5,max=5}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[277]},{t="h1",x="Survival",sub=S[353]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Single-target PvE Survival: a petless melee-and-trap build with Predator's Edge, Expose Prey and Lacerating Strikes, where Mongoose Bite carries the bleed damage, backed by Careful Aim, Lone Wolf and Lightning Reflexes. Not built for PvP or AoE farming."},{t="pills",list={"5 / 11 / 35 · 51 points at level 60",S[189],S[317]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[484]},{t="h2",x=S[214]},{t="p",x=S[49]},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Keep ranged openings"},{t="p",x="Train a pet and use it while the melee toolkit develops; Lone Wolf is taken late. Improved Tracking reaches 5/5 by level 14 and Survivalist 5/5 by 19. Do not force melee against enemies you could safely weaken at range."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Build the melee core"},{t="p",x="Surefooted is 3/3 by 22, Savage Strikes 2/2 by 24 and Predator's Edge 5/5 by 29. Strider Kick arrives at 30, Expose Prey is 2/2 by 32, Resourcefulness 2/2 by 34 and Lightning Reflexes 5/5 by 39. Deterrence and Counterattack remain unselected. Use actual weapons and mana recovery to judge the transition to melee."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Finish Survival, then Marksmanship and Beast Mastery"},{t="p",x="Lacerating Strikes at 40 completes the 31-point core. The last twenty points finish Survival (Clever Traps and Survivalist's Discipline, 41–44), then take Marksmanship (Lethal Attacks, Careful Aim and Lone Wolf, 45–55), then Deadly Aspects (56–60). Lone Wolf at 55 is when petless play begins; a leveling pet stays useful until then."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[248]},{t="h2",x="5 / 11 / 35 at level 60"},{t="p",x=S[64]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[286]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[233]},{t="p",x="Spend one point per level in each range. Unlisted talents stay at zero. This sequence has been checked against the calculator for totals, maximum ranks, tier gates and named prerequisites. After Lacerating Strikes at 40, the last twenty points finish the Survival tree, then take Marksmanship, then Beast Mastery."},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="|cffffffffBuilt for single-target PvE.|r This allocation is tuned for one enemy at a time: questing elites, dungeon bosses and raid-style boss fights. It is not a PvP build and not an area-damage (AoE) farming build; Deterrence, Counterattack and the control talents are not taken, and the traps are single-target damage tools rather than pack control."},{t="p",s="notice",x="All 51 points are assigned. Savage Strikes 2/2 and Lacerating Strikes 1/1 are part of this build: Mongoose Bite applies the Lacerating Strikes bleed (40% of the hit over 21 seconds), and Deterrence and Counterattack remain at zero. Lone Wolf, Careful Aim and Lethal Attacks come from Marksmanship, and Deadly Aspects from Beast Mastery."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[354]},{t="h2",x=S[264]},{t="p",x="Survival fights in melee, so your melee weapon matters as much as your bow. Agility is your main stat, with Strength adding melee attack power."},{t="h3",x=S[454]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[367],x="melee and ranged"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Agility",x=S[244]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Strength",x="melee attack power"},{t="p",s="small",x="Keep a decent ranged weapon for pulling, but put upgrades into your melee weapon first."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[367],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=3,b=S[433],x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b=S[532],x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Strength and Intellect are useful extras: Strength for melee attack power, Intellect for mana and Careful Aim."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Melee hit cap: 8% for special attacks against raid bosses. Expertise removes dodge at 6.5% and parry at 14% (parry only matters from the front). The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[265]},{t="h2",x=S[455]},{t="p",x=S[57]},{t="h4",x="Prepare the selected setup"},{t="p",x="Track the target's creature type, apply Hunter's Mark to support Expose Prey, and use Aspect of the Beast for melee: with Deadly Aspects, your melee auto attacks have a 10% chance to raise melee attack speed by 30% for 12 seconds. Lone Wolf gives 20% more damage with all attacks while you have no active pet, so go petless once you have it. Keep a ranged weapon for pulls and unsafe melee windows."},{t="h4",x="Keep melee attacks running"},{t="p",x="Use Raptor Strike and Strider Kick as available (Strider Kick deals 100% weapon damage and raises movement speed by 30% for 3 seconds), and use Mongoose Bite when enabled, including through Expose Prey, which gives attacks against a Hunter's Mark target a 10% chance to allow it for 10 seconds. Predator's Edge adds 30% critical damage to melee abilities and 50% Off Hand damage. Savage Strikes is a passive melee investment, not an extra button."},{t="h4",x="Account for the Mongoose Bite bleed"},{t="p",x="Lacerating Strikes triggers through Mongoose Bite; it is not a separate ability to cast. Its damage over time has more opportunity to contribute on durable, bleed-susceptible targets. Do not assume that delaying a ready Mongoose Bite to avoid refreshing the bleed is optimal: exact refresh behavior and level-60 priorities still need current-build testing."},{t="h4",x="Use traps and mana support"},{t="p",x="Use damaging traps for single-target damage when the target will remain in them. Clever Traps adds 30% damage to Immolation and Explosive traps, Survivalist's Discipline cuts trap cooldowns by 40%, and Resourcefulness cuts the mana cost of Trap and melee abilities by 60%. All of your traps share one 30-second cooldown, so pick the trap that fits the pull."},{t="h4",x="Stay safe and retain range"},{t="p",x="Counterattack and Deterrence are not selected. Do not include Counterattack in this rotation or seek boss attacks to trigger reactions. Switch to ranged attacks when mechanics prevent safe melee uptime. Careful Aim also turns Intellect into Attack Power, which helps every attack."},{t="h4",x=S[303]},{t="p",x="This build is for questing elites, dungeon bosses and boss fights, not for PvP or for farming packs. In groups, leave pack damage to others and keep your melee and bleed on your boss target."},{t="abil",names={"Raptor Strike","Mongoose Bite",S[411],S[485],S[486],"Aimed Shot","Arcane Shot",S[487],"Feign Death"}},{t="h3",x=S[378]},{t="p",x="Compare damage range, weapon speed, useful stats, requirements and your actual equipped item. Ranged-only bonuses do not improve melee attacks. Agility remains useful; this build also invests in Careful Aim (5/5), which turns Intellect into Attack Power for every attack, and Surefooted gives 3% hit. Do not apply a generic hit number to every encounter or attack type: check the current rules for your target and weapons before removing Surefooted."},{t="p",x=S[46]},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[326]},{t="h2",x=S[327]},{t="p",x=S[45]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="macro",n=S[208],x=S[70],code=S[154]},{t="macro",n=S[266],x=S[75],code=S[135]},{t="macro",n=S[488],x=S[67],code=S[278]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[97],code=S[304]},{t="macro",n="Mend Pet",x=S[89],code=S[150]},{t="macro",n=S[225],x=S[60],code=S[102]},{t="macro",n=S[226],x=S[61],code=S[109]},{t="macro",n="Wing Clip",x=S[78],code=S[112]},{t="macro",n="Mongoose Bite and melee attack",x="Start melee attacks and use Mongoose Bite when available. The selected Lacerating Strikes talent supplies its bleed; there is no separate Lacerating Strikes cast in this macro.",code="#showtooltip Mongoose Bite\n/startattack [harm,nodead]\n/cast [harm,nodead] Mongoose Bite"},{t="macro",n=S[411],x="Requires the selected Strider Kick talent. Keep it separate from damage buttons so you can hold it for the moment you need it.",code="#showtooltip Strider Kick\n/cast [harm,nodead] Strider Kick"},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[435]},{t="h2",x=S[234]},{t="p",x=S[42]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[51]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[267]},{t="h2",x=S[227]},{t="p",x=S[44]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[287]},{t="h2",x=S[215]},{t="p",x=S[40]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[268]},{t="h2",x=S[201]},{t="p",x=S[41]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[243]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[58]}}}},dungeons={{n=S[188],lr="13–18",st=S[94],no=S[43],ba=false,ra={ck=S[69],r={},t={},no={S[17],S[2]}}},{n=S[335],lr="13–18",st=S[279],no=S[86],ba=false,ra={ck=S[69],r={},t={},no={S[17],S